6. Tools and artifacts downloaded from upstream
------------------------------------------------

The following components are not part of the Ripley source tree or Ripley CLI
binary. Ripley downloads them from their upstream distributors into the local
user toolchain cache. Their own licenses continue to apply.

* darwin-tools-linux-llvm, from xtool-org
  Source: https://github.com/xtool-org/darwin-tools-linux-llvm
  Wrapper/build repository: MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 Kabir Oberai.
  The distributed ld64.lld, dsymutil, and llvm-libtool-darwin binaries are built
  from LLVM and are subject to Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception and applicable
  third-party LLVM notices.

* zsign
  Source: https://github.com/zhlynn/zsign
  License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 zhlynn.
  Ripley downloads the pinned upstream Linux release asset and verifies its
  SHA-256 before installing it into the local toolchain cache.

* Dart SDK and Flutter engine artifacts
  Sources: https://github.com/dart-lang/sdk and https://github.com/flutter/flutter
  Primary project licenses: BSD-3-Clause, with additional third-party licenses
  applying to bundled artifacts. Ripley downloads these artifacts from the
  upstream Dart/Flutter distribution infrastructure rather than redistributing
